# Workspace sandbox baseline. Do not commit filled-in credentials.
# Local testing and hosted dev/Preview staging reuse this Stripe sandbox account.
# Production uses separate live credentials: see .env.production.example.
# Local testing: npm run local:prepare generates localhost Supabase settings.
# It copies only the sandbox Stripe key from this file, not hosted database credentials.
# Local Pages API: copy the backend values to .dev.vars (Wrangler does not
# automatically load API secrets from .env.local).
# Local email Worker: copy its shared/backend and Brevo values to workers/.dev.vars.
# Production: set VITE_* as Pages build variables; set backend/Worker values
# as secrets on their respective Cloudflare deployments.

# Use .env.staging.example for hosted staging; local testing keys are generated separately.
# PUBLIC FRONTEND — embedded in browser JavaScript
VITE_APP_ENV=staging
# Supabase project URL and public publishable key (legacy anon key also works).
# Never put a Supabase service-role key in a VITE_* variable.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR_PUBLIC_ANON_OR_PUBLISHABLE_KEY

# SHARED BACKEND — required by both Pages API and scheduled email Worker
APP_ENV=staging
SUPABASE_DB_SCHEMA=staging
# Local URL below; use your canonical HTTPS site origin in production.
SITE_URL=http://localhost:8788
SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT.supabase.co
# Supabase service-role key; server-only, never included in the frontend.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# PAGES API ONLY — Stripe and QR credentials
# Use a dedicated Stripe sandbox during development. Prefer a restricted key
# with the required Checkout Sessions, Coupons, Prices, and Charges permissions.
# Catalog pricing requires Products/Prices read+write; checkout also needs Checkout/Coupons write and Charges read.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# Signing secret for /api/stripe-webhook (whsec_...). For local testing,
# use the secret printed by stripe listen, not the production endpoint secret.
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# Keep stable across deployments: changing this invalidates existing QR codes.
QR_SIGNING_SECRET=

# EMAIL WORKER ONLY — Brevo transactional email
BREVO_API_KEY=
# An email address verified as a sender in Brevo.
BREVO_SENDER_EMAIL=

# Additional setup, not application environment variables:
# - Configure Supabase Auth SMTP and the six-digit OTP email template in Supabase.
# - Configure Startup/Investor Stripe Price IDs and amounts in ticket_prices.
# - Provision admin/check-in roles in event_staff; there is no admin password.
